  Under Assumptions \ref{ass:c2}, \ref{ass:regularity}, there exist neighborhoods $\mathbb{P}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{\bl}$ of $\bp^\star$ and $\bbZ\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{\bn}$ of $\bz^\star$ and a continuous function $\bz^\dag:\mathbb{P}\rightarrow \bbZ$ such that $\bz^\dag(\bp)$ is a primal-dual solution of $P(\bp)$ that satisfies SSOSC and LICQ. Furthermore, for any $\bq:=\{q_i\}_{i\in \cV}\in\mathbb{R}^{\bl}$, the one-sided directional derivative of $\bz^\dag(\cdot)$ is given by:
